# Ptolemy's second theorem — for a cyclic quadrilateral the ratio of the diagonals: AC·(AB·BC + CD·DA) = BD·(AB·AD + BC·CD) (source: Ptolemy, Almagest)
A B C = triangle
D = reflect(C, perp_bisector(A, B))
prove dist(A, C) * (dist(A, B) * dist(B, C) + dist(C, D) * dist(D, A)) = dist(B, D) * (dist(A, B) * dist(A, D) + dist(B, C) * dist(C, D))
